      "side": 1,
      "message": "Could we add a README.md to the pkcs11 folder and among other things include the following markdown?\n\n\nWith the current `extract_logs` implementation,\nlogs are appended to the file at `$AUDIT_LOG_PATH`\nwhich is set by calling scripts.\nIf a directory is not specified, logs are placed in `$YUBIHSM_LOGS_DIR`, which defaults to the `logs/` subdirectory of the current working directory.\n\nAn example of an audit log name in the current scheme is `25610200-hawao-unknown-hsm-20250917-173949-release-audit.log`, where the components are `${BUILD_NUMBER}-${DEVICE}-${HSM_MODEL}-${HSM_SERIAL}-${DATE}-${TIME}-${COMMAND}-audit.log`.\n\nAny line beginning with `Hex: ` represents the hexadecimal log content at the time of extraction, and any line beginning with `item: ` contains the ASCII representation. (Both of these formats are included for flexibility.)",
